+## Part 1.5 — the self-direction mechanism (what the harness did when it did not know what to do next)
+
+This is the directive's second clause, and it is the transferable core.
+From the paper and the blog, when AVO's agent did not know what to do
+next it had exactly five moves. The structure is two nested loops around
+a persistent scored archive, with ground truth always available:
+
+1. **Re-read the lineage.** Every committed version persists with its
+   score (a git commit per version). The stuck agent "frequently examines
+   multiple prior implementations", compares their profiles, and locates
+   a bottleneck or an abandoned branch worth resuming.
+2. **Consult the knowledge base.** The agent pulls CUDA guides, PTX ISA,
+   Blackwell specs, or FlashAttention-4 source on demand. It chooses what
+   to read; nobody schedules it.
+3. **Measure at will.** The evaluation function is always on tap. The
+   agent runs edit-evaluate-diagnose cycles and commits only
+   improvements. Correctness is a hard gate; a wrong kernel scores zero.
+4. **Diagnose failures.** The agent reads compiler and profiler output,
+   forms a causal story, and revises. For ARC the same micro-loop is:
+   form a hypothesis, act, observe evidence, update state, continue.
+5. **Escalate to the supervisor.** When moves 1-4 plateau — a stall or an
+   unproductive repeat cycle — a second agent re-reads the WHOLE
+   trajectory and proposes several candidate strategic directions. The
+   main agent resumes along one.
+
+The self-direction is the freedom to pick which move to make next.
+In AVO a frontier model exercises that freedom. That is the exact point
+where the Qwen3.8-27B constraint bites, move by move:
+
+| AVO move | On Qwen3.8-27B | Concrete substitute on the live path |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1. Re-read the lineage | Survives, with the CHOICE moved to the harness | The model cannot browse an archive open-endedly. The harness curates what it re-reads: seeded repair hands the failed engine plus its mismatch report back as candidate zero (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6410/6470); playbook retrieval serves stuck-situation exemplars; the compacted carried state keeps refetch keys (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6540 line). |
+| 2. Consult the knowledge base | Does not carry at runtime | The scored run is offline, and reading hidden-game source is forbidden. Substitute: compile the knowledge into the harness at design time — solver-kit primitives, general gotchas, verifier features. This is KernelPro's expert-surrogate-as-tools idea, applied before the run instead of during it. |
+| 3. Measure at will | Survives outright — our strongest card | The verifier trust gate and offline replay are cheap, so the harness measures EVERY candidate. The decision "when to benchmark" leaves the model entirely: the answer is always. |
+| 4. Diagnose failures | Partially survives | A 27B model cannot reliably free-form diagnose. Substitute: mechanical mismatch reports (the tool loop's visible-mismatch report) name the defect; the model's job narrows to local repair of a named defect, not open diagnosis. |
+| 5. Supervisor | Detection survives; direction-proposal does not | Stagnation detection is model-free trajectory statistics — built as `TrajectorySupervisor` (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6600). Open-ended "propose a new strategy" is replaced by a closed decision table over existing levers; a later increment can select arms by run-local measured outcome (the `RunLocalMechanicLedger` pattern) instead of fixed order. |
+
+The summary inversion: AVO concentrates all decision-making in the model
+and gives it freedom. Our adaptation moves the decisions into mechanical
+harness components and spends the 27B model only where novel content must
+be generated — hypothesis and program text — always seeded with lineage,
+always scored mechanically. That inversion IS the method adoption under
+the model constraint; it is not a weaker copy of AVO, it is the same two
+nested loops with the intelligence budget reallocated.
+
+What each piece maps to on the live path today:
+
+- Inner loop (moves 3-4): induce -> `WorldModelVerifier` trust gate ->
+  `plan_in_model`; repair tool loop with seed and mismatch report.
+- Archive (move 1): engine store, induction attempt rows, go-explore
+  archive, playbook.
+- Outer loop (move 5): `TrajectorySupervisor` — the piece this note's
+  build adds; before it, the live agent had no counterpart at all.
+- Move 2 has no runtime form; its budget goes into design-time kit
+  primitives.
+
