+### Reframe check (same day, after the operator directive)
+
+The directive narrowed scope to the live agent and elevated the
+self-direction method. The build choice was re-examined against both and
+stands:
+
+- It is on the scored path: wired into `E3AgentPolicy._next_move_routed`,
+  reachable from both live entrypoints.
+- It is the outer half of the two-loop method (Part 1.5, move 5) — the
+  exact answer to "what did the harness do when it did not know what to
+  do next". The inner half (moves 3-4) already exists on the live path
+  as the trust gate plus the repair tool loop.
+
+### Next increments, in priority order
+
+1. **Lineage-aware arm selection.** The supervisor's snapshot carries no
+   attempt OUTCOMES yet. Feeding it the induction attempt rows lets the
+   decision table skip an arm the run already measured as useless — the
+   `RunLocalMechanicLedger` pattern, applied to arms.
+2. **Redirect receipts into the reinduction prompt.** A
+   supervisor-triggered reinduction should tell the generator what was
+   already tried and why it was redirected — AVO's lineage-visibility,
+   in bounded form.
+3. **The `qwen3_xml` parser trial** (blocked on Kaggle quota). It
+   unblocks in-loop tool calls on the scored backend, which is the
+   agent-as-operator inner loop AVO uses for kernels.
+
